@ Index:  Real-axis crossing of a complex segment from Y to X
@ Author: Jaco Mostert
@ Tested: Segment 1+i (parameter 0) to 3-i (parameter 1) crosses the real axis at 2.
@ Input:  Y = 1+i, X = 3-i
@ Output: X = 2
@
@ I is the value at parameter 0 and J the value at 1. SOLVE drives
@ xx over [0, 1] until FF, the imaginary part of the linear
@ interpolation, is zero. The real part of that point is kept in K.
LBL ‘PP’
  STO J             ; segment end, parameter 1
  DROP𝑥
  STO I             ; segment start, parameter 0
  DROP𝑥
  PGMSLV ‘FF’
  0                 ; lower guess
  1                 ; upper guess
  SOLVE ‘xx’
  RCL K
  Re                ; value at the crossing
  RTN

LBL ‘FF’
  RCL I
  RCL J
  RCL ‘xx’
  LINPOL
  STO K
  Im                ; residual for the solver
  END
.END.
